"""Used-oil EPR post: update of 12 Nov 2026. posts/ -> out/update-2026-11-12-indias-used-oil-epr-wants-half-of-all.html
New: PIB Parliament answer (EPR status as on 5 Mar 2026), MoEF&CC OM of 27 Aug 2026 (annual-return deadline),
CPCB annual-return guidance (Jan 2026), Petronas-Tata Motors pilot (PTI, 10 Sep 2026)."""
import pathlib

ROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]
SLUG = "indias-used-oil-epr-wants-half-of-all"
t = (ROOT / f"posts/{SLUG}.html").read_text()

TARGET_2425 = 68946
CERT_T, RECYCLED_T, RECYCLERS = 2000, 19000, 103     # PIB: 0.02 lakh MT, 0.19 lakh MT, as on 5 Mar 2026
assert round(CERT_T / TARGET_2425 * 100) == 3

PIB = "https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2244104&lang=1&reg=1"
OM = "https://www.ricago.com/assets/front/base/file/file_management/7228.pdf"
GUIDE = "https://eprusedoil.cpcb.gov.in/public/assets/images/Guidance%20Document%20for%20Submission%20of%20Annual%20Return%20by%20Registered%20Producers%20on%20Used%20Oil%20EPR%20Portal.pdf"
PTI = "https://manufacturing.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/energy/petronas-lubricants-tata-motors-collaborate-for-pilot-used-lubricant-recycling-model/133991516"


def rep(old, new):
    global t
    assert t.count(old) == 1, old[:80]
    t = t.replace(old, new)


NOTE = ('<div class="warn" style="border-left:4px solid #a5402c;background:rgba(165,64,44,.07);padding:.8em 1em;margin:1.2em 0;border-radius:4px">'
        '<b>Updated 12 November 2026.</b> The first national figures on what the scheme has actually recycled are now out. '
        f'In a Parliament answer, the environment ministry gave used-oil EPR&rsquo;s status as on 5 March 2026: {RECYCLERS} registered recyclers, about {RECYCLED_T:,} tonnes of used oil recycled '
        f'and about {CERT_T:,} tonnes of EPR certificates generated, against a 2024-25 target of {TARGET_2425:,} tonnes. '
        'The deadline for producers&rsquo; and recyclers&rsquo; annual returns for 2025-26 has since been extended from 30 June to 30 November 2026. '
        'A <a href="#eighteen-months">new section</a> sets this out. The registration counts below are still those of 10 August 2026: '
        'the portal&rsquo;s dashboard could not be re-read for this update.</div>\n')

rep('<span>Producer registrations granted vs applications received, as of writing</span>', '<span>Producer registrations granted vs applications received, on 10 August 2026</span>')
rep('<div class="stat"><b>IS 18722:2024</b><span>BIS standard for Re-refined Base Oil, published ~10 months after the EPR rules</span></div>\n</div>\n',
    '<div class="stat"><b>IS 18722:2024</b><span>BIS standard for Re-refined Base Oil, published ~10 months after the EPR rules</span></div>\n'
    f'<div class="stat"><b>~{CERT_T:,} t</b><span>EPR certificates generated by 5 March 2026, about 3% of the 2024-25 target (Parliament answer)</span></div>\n</div>\n'
    + NOTE)

SECTION = f'''<h2 id="eighteen-months">Eighteen months in, about 2,000 tonnes of certificates</h2>
<p class="h2sub">The first official count of what the scheme has delivered.</p>

<p>In a written answer to Parliament, published by PIB, the environment ministry set out the status of every EPR scheme as on 5 March 2026. Used oil had {RECYCLERS} registered recyclers. They had recycled about 0.19 lakh tonnes of used oil, roughly {RECYCLED_T:,} tonnes, and been issued EPR certificates for about 0.02 lakh tonnes, roughly {CERT_T:,} tonnes. The obligation for 2024-25 alone was {TARGET_2425:,} tonnes, so certificates covered about 3% of the first year&rsquo;s target, eleven months into the second year. The answer does not say whether the recycled tonnage includes oil processed before recyclers registered, or why so little of it had turned into certificates.</p>
<p>Used oil is by far the smallest of the five schemes in that table. Waste tyres had 579 recyclers and certificates for 116.94 lakh tonnes; plastic packaging, 2,986 recyclers and 196.97 lakh tonnes. Plastic, as noted below, already had a working collection market before its rules arrived. Used oil, as the industry panel described above, is still waiting for re-refined base oil to cost less than virgin oil.</p>
<p>The reporting cycle has slipped as well. Producers file annual returns on the portal, which reconcile their target against the certificates they hold; CPCB&rsquo;s guidance, dated January 2026, had them start with 2024-25. On 27 August 2026 the ministry extended the deadline for 2025-26 returns from 30 June to 30 November 2026, after CPCB reported requests from producers and recyclers citing &ldquo;operational and technical challenges&rdquo; in compiling and reconciling the data. Until those returns are in, nobody outside CPCB can say how much of either year&rsquo;s target was met, or how much Environmental Compensation is owed for the gap.</p>
<p>Some producers are building collection themselves rather than waiting. In September 2026 Petronas Lubricants India and Tata Motors announced a pilot in Maharashtra and Tamil Nadu that uses Tata&rsquo;s authorised service network to collect used lubricant and send it to registered recyclers for re-refining.</p>

'''
rep('<h2>Registration itself is tiered and non-trivial</h2>', SECTION + '<h2>Registration itself is tiered and non-trivial</h2>')

rep("so compliance against the 68,946-tonne 2024&ndash;25 target can be checked rather than assumed.</li>",
    f"so compliance against the 68,946-tonne 2024&ndash;25 target can be checked rather than assumed. The only official figure so far, about {CERT_T:,} tonnes of certificates by March 2026, came in a Parliament answer, not from the portal.</li>")

SRC = (f' &middot; Update of 12 November 2026: <a href="{PIB}">PIB, Parliament question &ldquo;Circular Economy Framework and Extended Producer Responsibility&rdquo;</a> (EPR status as on 5 March 2026) '
       f'&middot; <a href="{OM}">MoEF&amp;CC office memorandum F. No. 12/136/2021-HSM, 27 August 2026</a> (annual-return deadline; copy hosted by a compliance firm) '
       f'&middot; <a href="{GUIDE}">CPCB, Guidance Document for Submission of Annual Return by Registered Producers, January 2026</a> '
       f'&middot; <a href="{PTI}">PTI via ETManufacturing, 10 September 2026</a> (Petronas&ndash;Tata Motors pilot). '
       'The portal dashboard and PPAC&rsquo;s import/export page could not be re-read for this update, so the registration counts and the PPAC table are unchanged.')
rep("accessed 10 August 2026. Analysed 10 August 2026.", "accessed 10 August 2026. Analysed 10 August 2026." + SRC)

out = ROOT / f"out/update-2026-11-12-{SLUG}.html"
out.write_text(t)
print("wrote", out.relative_to(ROOT))
